IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgia-p1-definitions`

-- Minors' Contracts Act 1987 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 1 April 2022 -- LAYER 1: THE INTERPRETATION ACT 1965 AS IT READS THIS ACT.
--
-- This Act has no interpretation section and no rule of reading of its own, so nothing here encodes a
-- rule of this Act.  Two words of it are read through the Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1), whose definitions
-- Commons already encodes (sgia-p1-definitions.l4, copied UNCHANGED from the Interpretation Act row; see
-- NOTES.md, "Dependencies"):
--   * "he" (ss 2(b), 3(1)(b)): "words importing the masculine gender include females";
--   * "a person" (s 3(1)(a)): "'person' and 'party' include any company or association or body of persons,
--     corporate or unincorporate".
-- Neither is read by the seat: a person asking whether the Act applies to them need not say their sex or
-- whether they are a company.  They are here so that the Act's own pronoun and noun are not left to
-- guesswork, and so that the reuse is tested.
--
-- The Interpretation Act's period and date rules (ss 10, 50 to 53) are not used: this Act counts no period
-- and runs no deadline, and its dates (9 April 1987, 12 November 1993) are compared with the day a contract
-- was made, not counted from an event.

§ `Reading the Act's words through the Interpretation Act`

DECLARE `Sex of a party` IS ONE OF
    Male
    Female
    `Neither male nor female`

-- src:42 | (b) the obligation is unenforceable against him (or he
-- src:43 | repudiates the contract) because he was a minor when
-- src:44 | the contract was made,
@ref s 2(b) "him", "he" (src:42-44); s 3(1)(b) "he"; Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) "words importing the masculine gender"
GIVEN sex IS A `Sex of a party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 2(b) and 3(1)(b) the masculine word he reaches the party` MEANS
    CONSIDER sex
    WHEN Male THEN JUST TRUE
        -- the word itself: "he" names a male; no rule of reading is needed
    WHEN Female THEN
        IF elem "females" (`what the Act names in defining` "words importing the masculine gender")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `Neither male nor female` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the Interpretation Act rule says words importing the masculine gender "include females" and names no one else

DECLARE `Kind of claimant` IS ONE OF
    Individual
    Company
    Association
    `Body of persons, corporate or unincorporate`
    `Another kind of claimant`

-- src:51 | (a) a person (the claimant) has after 9 April 1987 entered into a
-- src:52 | contract with another (the defendant); and
@ref s 3(1)(a) "a person" (src:51-52); Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) "person"
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of claimant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(a) the Act's word a person reaches the claimant` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN Individual THEN JUST TRUE
        -- the ordinary meaning of "person"; the Interpretation Act definition "includes" and so only adds to it
    WHEN Company THEN
        IF elem "any company" (`what the Act names in defining` "person")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN Association THEN
        IF elem "association" (`what the Act names in defining` "person")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `Body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` THEN
        IF elem "body of persons" (`what the Act names in defining` "person")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `Another kind of claimant` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the Interpretation Act says "person" and "party" "include" a company, an association and a body of persons; it does not close the list
